invariant: INV-36
file: Makefile
catches: test/lint-trust-separation.sh
reason: the Makefile stops telling a device client from a host product, so
  a raw or ca client on an arm64 or x86-64 compiler builds the host
  object, -DCH_CPU_RUNTIME and ch_cfg.cpu included, and the default make
  lib grows a field every firmware caller would have to set
  (docs/decisions.md 89). lint-trust-separation's host rows require the
  four device clients to define no -DCH_CPU_RUNTIME under HOST_TARGET=yes.

--- old
DEVICE_CLIENT := $(filter client-raw-rsa client-raw-ecdsa client-ca-rsa client-ca-ecdsa,$(ROLE)-$(TRUST))
--- new
DEVICE_CLIENT :=
